  "description": "Dear Team,\n\nPlease find below the current container configuration for our two primary services. The web service runs an **nginx:latest** image under the container name **nginx_web**. It exposes port **8080** on the host and maps it to port **80** inside the container. The environment is set to production with `APP_ENV=production`, debugging disabled (`DEBUG=false`), and a maximum of **1000** connections (`MAX_CONNECTIONS=1000`). Static content is mounted from the local directory `./html` to `/usr/share/nginx/html` inside the container. The container is configured to always restart, and we have added the `NET_ADMIN` capability. It carries two labels\u2014`com.example.project=webapp` and `com.example.version=1.2.3`\u2014and resolves the internal host name **host.internal** to **10.0.0.5** via extra hosts. Logging uses the **json-file** driver with a maximum size of **10\u202fMiB** and up to three rotated files. The container starts with the command `nginx -g 'daemon off;'`, runs with a TTY attached, and does not keep stdin open.\n\nThe database service uses the **postgres:13** image, named **postgres_db**, and binds host port **5432** to the same port inside the container. Its environment variables are supplied as a list: `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=examplePassword`, `POSTGRES_DB=mydatabase`, and `POSTGRES_USER=admin`. Persistent data is stored on the host at `./pgdata`, mounted to `/var/lib/postgresql/data` in the container. The restart policy is **unless\u2011stopped**. Memory is limited to **512\u202fMiB**, with a swap limit of **1\u202fGiB**, and all capabilities are explicitly dropped (`ALL`). Security is tightened with the `no-new-privileges` option, and the container advertises the hostname **db.local**. Logging is directed to a syslog server via the **syslog** driver, using the address `tcp://192.168.1.100:514`. This container runs without a TTY and does not keep stdin open."
